      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "686ab487_d462a7f7",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/ProtectedData.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115498
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-27T17:49:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that `Configuration Hash` is generated directly from `Configuration Descriptor`, and only `Configuration Descriptor` is required in open-DICE, maybe we should just go ahead and make `Configuration Hash` optional here as well.\n\nThoughts?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "12abac21ccec397b59f9724d12d7088f5208c6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5a3b3cd_ba5c3758",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/ProtectedData.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-27T21:20:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on my read of Open Profile, Configuration Hash should not be omitted if it\u0027s mixed into the derivation of CDI. I think we\u0027re always mixing in H(Configuration Descriptor), so technically it\u0027s required for our implementation.\n\nHowever, it all seems like a bit of a wash. It\u0027s impossible to verify _what_ gets mixed into the CDI so I really don\u0027t see a purpose for carrying hashes in this data structure.",
      "parentUuid": "686ab487_d462a7f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "12abac21ccec397b59f9724d12d7088f5208c6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
