    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "78c4ce50_63129a1b",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/ProtectedData.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 154,
      "author": {
        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-27T21:20:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that we don\u0027t care about authority, I thought we\u0027d be ok without it (despite the fact that open profile requires it).",
      "parentUuid": "b0ec5eee_25a4814e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 154,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 154,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "12abac21ccec397b59f9724d12d7088f5208c6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9753a328_f767674f",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/ProtectedData.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 154,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115498
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-28T04:18:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why would we not care about authority? In this case I expect vendors to either insert the public key tied to Secure Boot or a fingerprint of that public key, either way.",
      "parentUuid": "78c4ce50_63129a1b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 154,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 154,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "12abac21ccec397b59f9724d12d7088f5208c6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "112fc4c4_9500b380",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/ProtectedData.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 154,
      "author": {
        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-28T17:01:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, but we\u0027re looking at code hashes and trust is ultimately in the root keys. In that case, it seems like authority doesn\u0027t matter. Unless, perhaps, there\u0027s a plan to start using authority in authorization policies?\n\nNote that I\u0027ve made it required to comply with Open Profile.\n\nThis would be a fun discussion to carry on off-CL.",
      "parentUuid": "9753a328_f767674f",
